+      "a": "1. WHO checklist, IV access, monitoring, suction, tilting trolley. 2. Pre-oxygenate 3 min with FiO₂ 1.0 to FetO₂ ≥ 0.9 (or 8 vital-capacity breaths). 3. Position: ramped/sniffing. 4. Low-flow nasal apnoeic oxygenation 15 L/min where appropriate; this is not high-flow THRIVE. 5. Pre-determined induction dose + neuromuscular blocker — no test dose, no bag-mask. 6. Consider cricoid pressure (10 N awake → 30 N once asleep) — release if view is poor or ventilation difficult. 7. Intubate, confirm sustained exhaled CO₂ (PUMA: rises with exhalation and falls with inspiration, consistent or increasing over at least seven breaths, peak > 1 kPa above baseline, clinically appropriate); if absent, actively exclude oesophageal intubation and remove the tube by default unless removal is judged more dangerous. Confirm tube depth separately. 8. Inflate cuff, secure tube, ventilate. 9. Use videolaryngoscopy first-line whenever possible for Plan A; have Plan B (second-generation SAD), Plan C (optimised facemask) and Plan D (eFONA) ready before induction (DAS 2025).",
