-      "a": "CICO = Can't Intubate, Can't Oxygenate: failed Plans A, B and C with falling SpO₂. Declare CICO out loud, stop further attempts, summon help and proceed immediately to scalpel-bougie-tube cricothyroidotomy — the trigger is failed oxygenation via tube, SAD and optimised facemask, not a saturation number. Technique: extend neck, palpate cricothyroid membrane, transverse stab with size 10 scalpel, rotate blade caudally, railroad a Frova/bougie, advance a 6.0 cuffed tube 2–3 cm, confirm with capnography. Needle cricothyroidotomy failed in > 60% of NAP4 emergencies and is no longer first-line.",
+      "a": "CICO = Can't Intubate, Can't Oxygenate: failed Plans A, B and C with falling SpO₂. Declare CICO out loud, stop further attempts, summon help and proceed immediately to scalpel-bougie-tube cricothyroidotomy — the trigger is failed oxygenation via tube, SAD and optimised facemask, not a saturation number. Technique (DAS 2025): extend the neck when appropriate. If cricothyroid-membrane anatomy was not explicitly assessed or remains uncertain, default to a midline vertical skin incision and expose/identify the membrane. A transverse approach is suitable only if the membrane is confidently identified or previously marked. Open the membrane with a size 10 scalpel, rotate the blade caudally, insert the bougie into the trachea and railroad a 6.0 cuffed tube; confirm ventilation with waveform capnography. Needle cricothyroidotomy failed in > 60% of NAP4 emergencies and is no longer first-line.",
