+      "a": "After 3 min of pre-oxygenation to FetO₂ ≥ 0.9, a fit non-obese adult tolerates ~8–10 min before SpO₂ falls below 90%. This shortens dramatically in obesity (3–4 min at BMI 40), pregnancy (2–3 min at term), sepsis, anaemia and small children (< 2 min in neonates). Apnoeic oxygenation with high-flow nasal cannulae (THRIVE, 70 L/min) or low-flow nasal cannulae (15 L/min) may extend apnoea tolerance depending on the patient and airway patency, but neither replaces pre-oxygenation or ventilation; CO₂ continues to accumulate — PaCO₂ rises by 3–4 mmHg/min.",
       "q": "How long can you safely be apnoeic after pre-oxygenation?",
     },
